※ pl4g-test: compile=ok
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=6
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4931 LANG_MUT_NEVER_CHANGED

※ Writing through a reference changes what it refers to, not the reference:
※ `r` is never made to refer anywhere else, so its own `mut` is reported.
※ `x`, written through `&mut`, is not.
let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let x: mut u6 = 5u6
    let r: mut &mut u6 = &x
    r⌖ ← r⌖ + 1u6
    x
